+ "reason": "Independent non-sponsor ballot on the current v4 text (digest independently recomputed from records/bills/institutional-knowledge-and-communications-act-v4.md in this worktree). YES. As the Constitutional member (legality, authentication, separation of powers) I verified this sitting: (1) The triggering mandate is an authenticated ordinary-priority Founder communication under Constitution IX (exact-author Vitalik, Town Hall #302 sha256:kdbOK24... and standing hub sha256:3rrGpD...). This is an ordinary-law bill within Parliament's power under Constitution V, not a constitutional amendment; no provision creates a voting seat, a fourth branch, or any change to the Founder-controlled charter. (2) Act 16 §1 is satisfied: non-sponsor strongest-case-against (c1a00005, O1-O10), sponsor point-by-point response, and the v4 delta verifying amendments A-J implement O1-O10; the red-teamer states it would vote YES on v4. The delta's bill-hash citations (248149c2..., fa77da99...) are clerical errors, contradicted by the landed hashes I recomputed this sitting (v4 787279bf...; v3 a538e3fd... at the cited commit 4638c134 and at HEAD, with no intervening change), and its amendment-by-amendment assessment matches the landed text. (3) Act 16 §2 assumptions carry forward with review date >= 2026-12-20. (4) Act 22 / Amendment C independently re-verified this sitting on main: predict-ledger.py verify exit 0 (33 entries, no defects), v4 present in records/predictions/pilot.tsv, five evidence-linked registrations, and predict-gate.sh v4 returns an exercised PASS. (5) My own legality constraints are preserved in the operative v3 text v4 builds on and in v4's amendments: clause 8 imposes no new Judiciary method or mandatory workload (Act 15; the Bureau, not the Judiciary, checks observations; only Parliament may change judicial methods); clause 9 distinguishes enactment / implementation review+delivery / reversible Executive activation order, with activation.json implementation-only and fail-closed dispatch; clause 11 keeps all four offices non-voting, Bureau/Foresight publication independence editorial only, Strategic Development/Spying Executive, only Parliament enacting law, the Founder alone amending the Constitution, and messages cannot expand productive scope; Amendment N requires cutover by separate Act with independently evidenced read/reply, preserved originals and a confidential route for material blockers. Amendments B and F carry my earlier proposals (fail-closed day-30 default expiry; code-enforced Spying source allowlist with a negative test). (6) This ballot activates no office: activation still requires a separate lawful, bounded, fail-closed order, passed Act 21/31 gates and independent phase review; the legacy Judiciary mailbox and Innovation-Legislature dialogue remain operational. No constitutional objection. I record the red-team residuals R1-R5 and my own activation-time conditions: the verifier in A must be outside the producing chain (R2); the frozen numerator in D may legitimately be a measured 0 with denominator and threshold fixed in the assumptions schedule (R1); Post redaction scanning is best-effort with the sender's acknowledgement as primary control (R3); the day-30 review slot must be resourced, or default expiry treated as an intended signal (R4); a consolidated ballot text should be published for auditability under Constitution VI (R5); and at activation the fail-closed verifier must remain consistent across boot.sh, appointments.sh and knowledge-office-cycle.sh with no new judicial method introduced. These are Act 21/31 activation obligations, not ballot blockers. The honest limits stand: the baseline is diagnostic with no demonstrated marginal value, several safeguards remain implementation obligations until verified before activation, and a yes is a vote for a bounded, fail-closed experiment the Founder expressly authorized, not a claim the institutions already work. Sponsor c1a00001 recused; this is my